   "source": [
    "## 2. VaR Models\n",
    "Four methods implemented at 99% confidence level:\n",
    "- **Historical Simulation** — empirical percentile of rolling returns\n",
    "- **Parametric (Variance-Covariance)** — assumes normally distributed returns\n",
    "- **Monte Carlo GBM** — simulates 10,000 paths using Geometric Brownian Motion\n",
    "- **Monte Carlo Student-t** — GBM with fat-tailed Student-t residuals (df=5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 102,
   "id": "771e1086-858d-4231-b2bc-2248762e9439",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "window= 252 \n",
    "confidence= 0.99\n",
    "\n",
    "hist_var = []\n",
    "hist_es= []\n",
    "hist_dates= []"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 103,
   "id": "e26e7303-493a-4a8c-a9d8-993d7ebbc5f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for i in range(window, len(log_returns)):\n",
    "    rolling_window = log_returns.iloc[i - window:i]\n",
    "    var= np.percentile(rolling_window, 100 - (confidence*100))\n",
    "    tail= rolling_window[rolling_window<= var]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if len(tail) >0:\n",
    "        hist_var.append(abs(var))\n",
    "        hist_es.append(abs(tail.mean()))\n",
    "        hist_dates.append(log_returns.index[i])\n",
    "        \n",
    "    \n",
    "    "
   ]
  },
